# Design System

## Colors
- Use ONLY CSS custom properties defined in your globals/tokens file. Never hardcode hex values.
- Prohibited color ranges: [LIST RANGES FROM DESIGN SPEC — e.g. "No red-family colors (#FF..., #E5..., #DC... ranges)"]
- Reason: [STATE WHY — e.g. "Avoid urgency cues in a calm productivity tool"]
- Palette tokens to use: [LIST YOUR TOKEN NAMES — e.g. --color-primary, --color-surface]

## Typography
- Heading font: [FONT NAME] — only for [heading roles]
- Body font: [FONT NAME] — for all body text
- Accent font: [FONT NAME or "none"] — only for [accent use cases]
- Do not introduce new font families without updating this rule

## Animation
- Maximum transition duration: [N]ms for micro-interactions, [N]ms for layout transitions
- Easing: [CURVE] for entrances, [CURVE] for exits
- Always provide a `prefers-reduced-motion` alternative:
  ```css
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    /* disable or simplify transitions */
  }
  ```

## Accessibility
- Every interactive element must have an accessible label (`aria-label` or associated `<label>`)
- Focus ring must be visible on keyboard navigation — do not suppress `:focus-visible` outlines
- Minimum touch target size: 44×44px for mobile targets
- Color contrast: minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text
